WEBVTT

00:00:00.650 --> 00:00:05.450
On the Mcbe2Friends project page, choose
the download for your computer.

00:00:05.620 --> 00:00:09.020
Extract the archive and open the
launcher. On Windows,

00:00:09.020 --> 00:00:12.596
open Mcbe2Friends.exe. The controls open
in your browser.

00:00:13.443 --> 00:00:16.921
Already have a running server? Enter its
Bedrock address and port.

00:00:17.091 --> 00:00:20.675
The usual port is 19132. Choose
Continue.

00:00:21.527 --> 00:00:25.431
Use a dedicated Microsoft account with
an Xbox gamertag.

00:00:25.601 --> 00:00:28.657
Choose whether to accept friend requests
automatically,

00:00:28.657 --> 00:00:30.315
then select Connect & start.

00:00:31.152 --> 00:00:34.658
The launcher sets up Java if needed.
When a code appears,

00:00:34.658 --> 00:00:36.613
choose Open Microsoft sign-in.

00:00:36.783 --> 00:00:40.260
Enter your own code on Microsoft’s page
and finish signing in.

00:00:41.110 --> 00:00:45.931
Wait for Broadcast live, then give
friends the broadcaster’s Xbox gamertag.

00:00:46.101 --> 00:00:50.180
Once their requests are accepted, they
open Minecraft Bedrock, choose Play,

00:00:50.180 --> 00:00:52.349
then Friends, and select your session.

00:00:53.193 --> 00:00:57.673
Keep the PC awake. Closing the browser
tab leaves the broadcast running.

00:00:57.843 --> 00:01:00.416
Use Stop broadcast to end it. Next time,

00:01:00.416 --> 00:01:02.814
Start broadcast reuses your settings.

00:01:03.652 --> 00:01:06.809
To host a new world on your own PC, open
Premium.

00:01:06.979 --> 00:01:11.053
Check your hardware and recommended
settings.

00:01:11.053 --> 00:01:15.043
Hosting supports Windows x64 and Ubuntu
x64.

00:01:15.902 --> 00:01:18.811
Copy your PC code, choose Get Premium on
Discord,

00:01:18.811 --> 00:01:20.787
and send the code to the seller.

00:01:20.957 --> 00:01:25.339
After the one-time $15 purchase, paste
the key you receive and choose

00:01:25.339 --> 00:01:26.120
Activate.

00:01:26.943 --> 00:01:29.495
Review the Minecraft terms, check the
box,

00:01:29.495 --> 00:01:31.658
then select Install & start server.

00:01:31.828 --> 00:01:35.433
The launcher applies the PC preset. Wait
for Server running.

00:01:36.277 --> 00:01:40.589
Under Players & Friends tab, enter a
friend’s Xbox gamertag and choose

00:01:40.589 --> 00:01:42.570
Allow. Repeat for each player.

00:01:42.740 --> 00:01:46.707
Players on your network can also join
using the local address and server

00:01:46.707 --> 00:01:47.177
port.

00:01:48.027 --> 00:01:53.494
For internet play, forward the server
port for both TCP and UDP to the host

00:01:53.494 --> 00:01:53.979
PC.

00:01:54.149 --> 00:01:56.420
Enter an address your friends can reach,

00:01:56.420 --> 00:01:59.311
then choose Friends setup and follow the
Xbox steps.

00:02:00.152 --> 00:02:02.840
While the server is running, open Server
console.

00:02:03.010 --> 00:02:05.356
Send the list command to see who is
online.

00:02:06.193 --> 00:02:09.073
Choose Stop server to save the world
before editing.

00:02:09.243 --> 00:02:12.360
Open Server settings & worlds. Choose a
world,

00:02:12.360 --> 00:02:16.411
adjust the player slots or use PC
recommendations, then save.

00:02:17.235 --> 00:02:21.084
Under Add-ons, choose your .mcaddon or
.mcpack file and click Import

00:02:21.084 --> 00:02:21.672
add-on.

00:02:21.842 --> 00:02:26.024
Enable each required resource and
behavior pack for the selected world.

00:02:26.860 --> 00:02:30.519
Under World imports & backups, choose
Back up selected world.

00:02:30.519 --> 00:02:32.940
Open backups to find the .mcworld file.

00:02:33.110 --> 00:02:37.663
If the old world folder still exists,
use Open server folder. In worlds,

00:02:37.663 --> 00:02:40.299
rename the old folder to keep your copy.

00:02:40.759 --> 00:02:44.495
Choose the .mcworld, enter the original
world name for the new folder,

00:02:44.495 --> 00:02:45.858
and click Import world.

00:02:46.693 --> 00:02:50.853
Select the restored world in settings,
save, and start the server again.

00:02:51.023 --> 00:02:53.567
With the host PC awake and the broadcast
live,

00:02:53.567 --> 00:02:55.653
your friends can get back to playing.

00:02:57.183 --> 00:03:00.597
Open Premium and choose Java Edition. Name your server.

00:03:00.867 --> 00:03:05.709
Choose Vanilla for Java, Paper for plugins, or Paper + Geyser for cross-play.

00:03:06.350 --> 00:03:10.574
Accept the Minecraft EULA and choose Create & start.

00:03:10.844 --> 00:03:17.306
Once it’s running, Java players use Multiplayer. Bedrock players use the Geyser port or the Friends setup.

00:03:17.933 --> 00:03:23.907
Stop the Paper server to import a trusted plugin JAR. Enable it, then start the server to load it.

00:03:24.177 --> 00:03:29.019
You can also switch Geyser on or off under Settings & cross-play and keep the same world.

00:03:29.642 --> 00:03:35.210
Back up a stopped world here, or restore a ZIP into a new folder. Select the world in Settings.

00:03:35.480 --> 00:03:40.109
Start your server and close the launcher. It keeps running while your computer stays awake.
